# NOTE 06: STREAMLIT & PLOTLY FRONTEND UI NOTES
## Complete Bit-by-Bit Study Guide & UI Examples for Zaika Restaurant Management System

================================================================================
1. HOW STREAMLIT POWERS ZAIKA'S 4 INTERFACES
================================================================================
Streamlit turns pure Python scripts into interactive web applications without requiring HTML, CSS, or JavaScript. Whenever a user clicks a button or selects a filter, Streamlit reruns the Python script from top to bottom.

Zaika's Multi-Page Frontend Architecture:
- `frontend/app.py`: Entry point. Checks URL query parameters (`?table=T1&token=...`) to launch the Customer Mobile QR Menu automatically, or renders the Staff/Kitchen/Owner Login screen.
- `frontend/pages/1_Customer_QR_Menu.py`: Mobile dish cards, Veg/Allergen/Search filters, interactive cart, live cooking timer, Free WiFi, 200-pt Mango Lassi progress bar, Spice Quiz, Table vs. Table leaderboard, and Call Waiter alert button.
- `frontend/pages/2_Staff_Floor_Map.py`: Live T1–T6 floor grid, pending customer order confirmation ("Send to Kitchen"), and Call Waiter alert resolver.
- `frontend/pages/3_Kitchen_Display.py`: 3-column KDS board (`Tandoor`, `Curry`, `Drinks`) with Green/Yellow/Red urgency timers.
- `frontend/pages/4_Billing_Checkout.py`: Itemized bill, 2/3/4 or per-item split calculator, tip selector, 5 payment methods, and post-payment 1–5 star review form.
- `frontend/pages/5_Owner_Dashboard.py`: Live KPI metrics, Plotly sales & top-dish charts, waiter SLA speed, and Menu/Staff management.

================================================================================
2. SESSION STATE (`st.session_state`) & QR QUERY PARAMS (`st.query_params`)
================================================================================
Because Streamlit reruns your script on every click, variables reset unless stored inside `st.session_state`.

```python
import streamlit as st

st.set_page_config(page_title="Zaika Restaurant", page_icon="🍛", layout="wide")

# Initialize persistent session variables
if "cart" not in st.session_state:
    st.session_state.cart = []            # List of selected dish dicts
if "jwt_token" not in st.session_state:
    st.session_state.jwt_token = None     # Staff/Kitchen/Owner Bearer token
if "user_role" not in st.session_state:
    st.session_state.user_role = None     # 'staff', 'kitchen', or 'owner'
if "table_info" not in st.session_state:
    st.session_state.table_info = None    # Verified QR table dict

# Read QR Code URL parameters: e.g., http://localhost:8501/?table=T1&token=tok_t1_99a1
params = st.query_params
qr_table = params.get("table")
qr_token = params.get("token")
```

