6. OWNER ANALYTICS WITH PLOTLY CHARTS (5_Owner_Dashboard.py)

Uses st.metric for top-level KPIs and plotly.express for interactive sales and dish-popularity charts.
```python
import streamlit as st
import pandas as pd
import plotly.express as px
from frontend.utils.api_client import api_get
st.title("📊 Owner Live Analytics Dashboard")
summary = api_get("/api/analytics/summary")
if summary:
k1, k2, k3, k4 = st.columns(4)
k1.metric("Tables Active", f"{summary['active_tables']}/6")
k2.metric("Total Orders Today", summary["total_orders_today"])
k3.metric("Total Sales Today", f"Rs.{summary['total_sales_today']:,.0f}")
k4.metric("Avg Customer Rating", f"{summary['avg_rating']:.1f} ⭐")
st.divider()
c_left, c_right = st.columns(2)
with c_left:
st.subheader("Hourly Live Sales")
sales_df = pd.DataFrame(summary["hourly_sales"])
fig_sales = px.line(sales_df, x="hour", y="revenue", markers=True, title="Revenue Today (Rs.)")
st.plotly_chart(fig_sales, use_container_width=True)
with c_right:
st.subheader("Top-Selling Dishes")
dishes_df = pd.DataFrame(summary["top_dishes"])
fig_dishes = px.bar(dishes_df, x="dish_name", y="total_sold", color="dish_name", title="Units Sold")
st.plotly_chart(fig_dishes, use_container_width=True)
```

